  "question": {
    "text": "An object viewed from a near point distance of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>25</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math>, using a microscopic lens with magnification <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn><mo>,</mo></math> gives an unresolved image. A resolved image is observed at infinite distance with a total magnification double the earlier using an eyepiece along with the given lens and a tube of length <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>, if the focal length of the eyepiece is equal to ____&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>cm</mi><mo>.</mo></math>"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "25",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>For simple microscope,<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>D</mi><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mfrac></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>D</mi><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mfrac></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>25</mn><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mfrac></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math></p><p>For compound microscope,<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>&#8467;</mi><mo>&#183;</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>&#183;</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>12</mn><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>60</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>25</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>&#183;</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>f</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>25</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math></p>"
  }
}